{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixHeap"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The radix heap of Ahuja, Mehlhorn, Orlin and Tarjan, in the form with one bucket per bit:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bucket ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds the keys whose highest bit differing from the last key removed is bit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"b - 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and bucket 0 the keys equal to it. ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is O(1). ","type":"text"},{"code":"popMin()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is O(1) when bucket 0","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds a pair; otherwise it empties the lowest nonempty bucket into lower ones. A pair moves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only to lower buckets, so it moves at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt.bitWidth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" times, and for keys spread over a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range of ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at most log₂ C + 1 times: amortized O(log C) a pop.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use it where keys never go below the last one removed, as in Dijkstra’s algorithm with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer weights. It has no decrease-key: insert the value again with the lower key and skip","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the stale pair when it comes out. Values with equal keys leave in an unspecified order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The queue is not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Storage is an array of bucket arrays, copied on write.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:19PriorityQueueModule9RadixHeapV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixHeap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixHeap"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"RadixHeap.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap.swift#L17"},"role":"symbol","title":"RadixHeap","modules":[{"name":"PriorityQueueModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A monotone min-priority queue of values with nonnegative integer keys, where no key inserted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is below the last key removed."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/priorityqueuemodule\/radixheap"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/init()"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/count","doc:\/\/PriorityQueue